{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779228182,"nonce":"N0vLE7mzjRJ00MbVyzZrMVNVyNo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABCxx1Ww","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/137","origin":"github"},"title":"M3 sonar: investigate intermittent missing pings (suspected ping-rate × depth correlation)","message":"## Observation\n\nMissing pings in M3 sonar data have been observed across multiple deployments. The 2026-05-19 deployment was the first time the M3 software's log window was open during ops, surfacing explicit `dropped packets` error messages alongside the data-side gaps Roland had previously noticed.\n\nObserved window with explicit log-side errors:\n\n- **2026-05-19** ≈ 13:42 EDT (Phase 1, on-water): M3 software reporting dropped packets in its log window. Boat was operating Starlink-only at the operator station, but M3 → mercat is on the boat's wired LAN, so the Starlink path is **not** in the M3 → mercat data flow. The Starlink correlation in the initial dev-side framing is a coincidence of when the log window happened to be open, not a cause.\n\n## Hypothesis (operator)\n\nLikely correlated with **ping rate × water depth** — historically not seen in shallower water. To investigate.\n\n## Investigation leads\n\n- **Pull the M3 log error messages** from salmon's screenshooter video capture in `~/data/logs` for the 2026-05-19T13:42–13:46 EDT window. That's the first time the explicit error text was captured.\n- **Cross-reference past sonar bags** with recorded depth and the M3 ping-rate setting at the time, to test the depth-correlation hypothesis.\n- **Mercat NIC counters / Wireshark** on the M3 ingress interface during a known-bad window, if reproducible — distinguishes NIC drop, socket-buffer drop, or upstream LAN loss.\n- **QINSy + AML bridge + RDP session contention** on mercat as a potential confounder — RDP-over-Starlink was active during 2026-05-19 ops.\n\n## Not blocking\n\nNot deploy-blocking for upcoming runs, but **load-bearing for the June 2026 hydro class** if missing pings scale up at the ping-rate × depth combos used for actual survey grids. Worth nailing the cause before the class.\n\n## Related\n\n- 2026-05-19 deployment: #135 (dev log corrective entry at 14:20; field-host gabby and salmon logs in the PR #136 bundle).\n- Memory of past sonar / M3 architecture: `project_bizzyboat_sonar_architecture` (workspace-side; M3 + mercat on boat, wired Ethernet).\n\nPart of #135\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}